Z||000000||1FST2M6||06-04-2001||08:27 AM||||  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> hey everyone... i'm back from our 8 day Honeymoon in WONDERFULLY SUNNY Montego Bay, Jamaica! stayed at Sandals Royal Caribbean. Pics to follow later in the week.. we took over 200 pics.. some i don't think i can post..   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> we went to Dunns River falls, in Ocho Rios, and went to Kingston for a day. it was really SWEET... street racing and @sshols doing burn outs in the Dunns river resort parking lots at 4am... fun to watch a Levin light em up... anywho. I just hope that our marriage is as strong as Hughs!  i'm sure it will be.. thanks to Black GT and RodRv6 for comming to the wedding and reception... i needed all the support i could get... not sure why i was SO nervous but D@MN was i feeling weak during the ceremony.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>I haven't dropped off the face of the earth.. just droped off the bachelor scene in to another realm. <P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig1fst.jpg">        <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A>  <A HREF="http://www.epdyno.com" TARGET=_blank>www.epdyno.com</A>  <A HREF="http://www.enthuzacar.com" TARGET=_blank>www.enthuzacar.com</A> <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 06-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||06-04-2001||08:45 AM||||Glad to see you back!  Best wishes to you and your wife!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
Z||000002||JSocha||06-04-2001||09:13 AM||||Congradulations!<P>Welcome to the world of no life with a wife!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Since you went up Dunn River Falls (BTW, how did you like the flea market at the top?  Nice place to put it huh?  Did you tell them "Me no want nothin man..."?) did you also go over to visit an old hotel which was turned into a flower garden (which had burned down)?  My wife loved that place.<P>We were in Jamica back in '98 on our Honeymoon when we did the Carabiean Cruise thing on Holland America.  I will never go back to Jamica and if we do, I will not get off the ship there again.<P>To me, it was like being at a "Lawyers Convention" and you being the only possible client.  They have their hands practically in your pockets the whole entire time.<P>I also believe one could possibly find many Fiero parts there as the people have almost every vehicle you can imagine dismantled in their yards and/or are living in them.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||6
Z||000003||1FST2M6||06-04-2001||09:35 AM||||the "EXIT" signs the lead you out of the market were just horrible misleading! i thought it was fun and SHE was really scared.. their all grabbin g your arms and at the SAME time "i respect you.. come see my shop"  at the same time we are say how can you respect me while your forcing me into somthing i don't want to do.. and the they cam back "what you don't like jamaicans?"  the tin shacks, and brightly painted wheelless buses as home are REALLy tough to get used to and to see people not willing to better themselves and live in that element. and to hear then claim "we got 3 or 4 kids and we neeed your business" blah blah blah..  i felt bad staying in a resort seeing their digs until i as at the market at dunns river, Falmouth and in Kingston... they arent' trying to better their situation, theyare just looking for a hand out or take what you have.. i got a New watch that reatils for over a grand here in the states and picked it up for under $400 in Ocho Rios and in the market everone wanted to take my watch for anything in their shop... uum it's 4 hours old NO...  and they are SO persistant. i'll go back to Jamaica.. but i wont leave the resort. we are planning a trip to Sandals Royal Bahamaian around Halloween this year... not sure how the culture is there but the resort is sweet looking... thanks for all your kind reguards guys!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>Hey RodrV6... when is dinner at LaPaz? <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 06-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Raydar||06-04-2001||09:49 AM||||Trav!<BR>Congrats to the both of ya'! <P>I've only been married for a little over three years (old fart that I am) and married life keeps getting better every day.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 06-04-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000005||JSocha||06-04-2001||10:01 AM||||Don't you know it!<P>When we were in Florida at the terminal waiting for our flight after the cruise, we met another couple who were at a resort in Jamica.<P>They left the resort and the safety of the 10' high chain link fences that surrond the place to check out the town.  BIG MISTAKE is what they told us.<P>From the moment they walked out (to which the gate guards informed them not to and to be careful) they were being hit up from everyone for money or to buy drugs, wooden beads, statues (with the b*n*rs sticking straight out) or anything else they could solicite.  They were never so happy to get back behind the fence and stated if they ever went back to Jamica, they would stay at and never leave the resort again.<P>We got to watch guards throw people out of the market place that were trying to get in with their stuff.<P>At Dunn River, after we got done going up the falls and ended up in the market place, they werre trying to get us into their huts.  I told one guy, we left our wallet's on the bus and he immidately offered to go back to the bus with us to get it.  Thats when I finally told him (based on what our tour guide told us to say) "Me no want nottin man" (which is the equivelant of saying "Back off" or "Leave me alone") to which he looked at me just amazed and said "You be insultin me mann!".  I told him I don't care, I don't want anything and to leave us alone.  Boy do they get vulgar!<P>Our tour guide at the end of the flower garden tour wouldn't let me by afterwards as he was waiting for a tip from me.  I pointed to my wife and said my wife has my wallet and just payed you a very large tip.  He looked at me then my wife, said a few choice words and let me by.<P>Also at the flower garden's and after the tour, I was taking pictures and I just happened to take a picture where a guy, dressed in Flowers next to a mule was standing (in front of the picture I was actually trying to get) and the moment he heard the sound of my camera go off, his hat came off as if I was to pay him for his picture.<P>Told him wife has the wallet, and he to was peed off and started swearing at me and that I should give him the film.<P>Nice place to visit, but I will never go there again or get off the ship if we do!<P>Got to see where James Bond's "Dr. No" was filmed (the warehouse scene) as well as the lagoon where Gilligans Island was filmed as our ship was docked in front of both places!<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||1FST2M6||06-04-2001||10:15 AM||||AAAGGH!! that guy is still there!!! the scary dude in a dress with the mule and flowers.. he wante $20 for a pic... luckily my camera zoom like crazy.. so we went and got the $110   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> single chocolate cones from baskin robins and snapped off a few of him.  and the signs of the "sleeping policemen" were pretty strange. the tour guds are paid by the cruise and the resorts NOT to bother you about $ and they still do.. "i've got kids" "your peoples donations help send them to school" uum NO.. i paid $140us for this trip.. i'm not dropping $300ja for a tip kiss my @ss.  out side our back door or out the bathroom window we could see a pblic peer where many natives would bath in the morning... soap and rags in their undies in the salt water... that was odd... and whats up with EVERONE haveing the SAME crap.. but they all carved it them selves "by hand" and the guy not 2 meters away has the SAME THING.. al "HAND CARVED" buy his "old dying hands"  yeah.. ok dude.. i'm going over here... and everone sounds like Jar-Jar Binks! and EVERYONE had a "special small bag" for us... uum no thanks.. <P>while everyone that works in the resort seemed well educated easy to understand and laid back... i guess the resorts must pay really well... <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 06-04-2001).]||||reg||1
